<p>t₁ = 120 / 60 = 2 hours</p>

<p><b>Stage 2:</b></p>
<p>t₂ = 80 / 40 = 2 hours</p>

<p><b>Total:</b></p>
<p>2 + 2 = <b>4 hours</b></p>

<h3>Worked Example 2</h3>

<p>
A cyclist travels 60 km at 20 km/h and then 45 km at 15 km/h.
</p>

<p><b>Stage 1:</b></p>
<p>t₁ = 60 / 20 = 3 hours</p>

<p><b>Stage 2:</b></p>
<p>t₂ = 45 / 15 = 3 hours</p>

<p><b>Total:</b></p>
<p>3 + 3 = <b>6 hours</b></p>

<h3>Worked Example 3</h3>

<p>
