<h2>Muscle Cell Adaptation</h2>

<h3>What makes a muscle cell specialised?</h3>

<p>
Muscle cells are specialised to contract and generate force.
This allows muscles to produce movement.
</p>

<h3>Contractile structures</h3>

<p>
Muscle cells contain specialised structures that can slide relative
to one another, causing the cell to shorten.
