<h3>Shoot system</h3>

<p>
The <b>shoot system</b> includes structures such as stems, leaves,
flowers and fruits.
</p>

<h3>Root system</h3>

<p>
The <b>root system</b> consists mainly of the roots. It anchors the
plant and absorbs water and mineral ions from the soil.
</p>

<h3>Why are these systems important?</h3>

<p>
Different plant organs depend on one another. For example, roots
absorb water and minerals while leaves use water during photosynthesis.
</p>

