    <b>A / a</b><br>
    <b>B / b</b>
  </p>

  <p>
    One possible arrangement can send <b>A</b> and <b>B</b> toward the same
    pole.
  </p>

  <p>
    Another possible arrangement can send <b>A</b> and <b>b</b> toward the
    same pole.
  </p>

  <p>
    Therefore, the chromosome combinations entering gametes can differ.
  </p>

  <h3>Do the chromosomes change?</h3>

