<p><b>Step 2:</b> Meiosis I separates homologous chromosome pairs.</p>

<p><b>Answer:</b> Homologous chromosomes separate and move towards opposite poles.</p>

<h3>Important distinction</h3>

<p>
Meiosis I separates <b>homologous chromosomes</b>, while Meiosis II later separates
<b>sister chromatids</b>.
