  (809, 809, '
  <h2>Probability in AA × Aa</h2>

  <h3>The cross</h3>

  <p>
    Let A be dominant over a.
  </p>

  <p>
    Cross:
  </p>

  <p>
    <b>AA × Aa</b>
  </p>

  <h3>Gametes</h3>

  <p>
    AA → <b>A</b>
  </p>

  <p>
    Aa → <b>A or a</b>
  </p>

  <h3>Possible offspring</h3>

  <p>
    A + A = <b>AA</b>
  </p>

  <p>
    A + a = <b>Aa</b>
  </p>

  <p>
    Therefore:
  </p>

  <p>
    <b>P(AA) = 1/2 = 50%</b>
  </p>

  <p>
    <b>P(Aa) = 1/2 = 50%</b>
  </p>

  <h3>Probability of aa</h3>

  <p>
    There is no way to produce aa.
  </p>

  <p>
    The first parent can only provide A.
  </p>

  <p>
    Therefore:
  </p>

  <p>
    <b>P(aa) = 0%</b>
  </p>

  <h3>Phenotype probability</h3>

  <p>
    Both AA and Aa have the dominant phenotype.
  </p>

  <p>
    Therefore:
  </p>

  <p>
    <b>P(dominant phenotype) = 100%</b>
  </p>

  <p>
    <b>P(recessive phenotype) = 0%</b>
  </p>
