  <p>
  Two organisms may mate but fail to produce fertile offspring. This means
  they are not necessarily members of the same species.
  </p>

  <p>
  For example, a horse and a donkey can produce a mule, but the mule is
  generally sterile. Therefore, horses and donkeys are classified as
  different species.
  </p>

  <h3>Important idea</h3>

  <p>
  Species classification is based on biological relationships, not simply
  physical appearance.
  </p>
