<h2>Ecosystem</h2>

<p>
An <b>ecosystem</b> consists of a community of organisms interacting with one another and with the non-living components of their environment.
</p>

<h3>Two major components</h3>

<p>
An ecosystem contains:
</p>

<ul>
<li><b>Biotic components</b> — living organisms.</li>
<li><b>Abiotic components</b> — non-living physical and chemical conditions.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Example</h3>

<p>
A pond ecosystem may contain:
</p>

<ul>
<li>fish</li>
<li>algae</li>
<li>insects</li>
<li>bacteria</li>
<li>water</li>
<li>oxygen</li>
<li>light</li>
<li>temperature</li>
</ul>

<p>
The organisms interact with one another and with the physical environment.
</p>

<h3>Building the idea</h3>

<p>
<b>Organisms of one species → population</b>
</p>

<p>
<b>Different populations → community</b>
</p>

<p>
<b>Community + abiotic environment → ecosystem</b>
</p>
