<h2>Abundance and Density</h2>

<h3>DEEP NOTES</h3>

<p>
<strong>Abundance</strong> refers to the amount or number of individuals of
a species found in a particular area or sample.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Density</strong> expresses the number of individuals per unit area
or volume.
</p>

<h3>DENSITY</h3>

<p>
<strong>
Density = number of individuals ÷ area
</strong>
</p>

<p>
