<h2>Nitrogen Cycle</h2>

<h3>DEEP NOTES</h3>

<p>
The <strong>nitrogen cycle</strong> describes how nitrogen moves between the
atmosphere, soil and living organisms.
</p>

<p>
Nitrogen is essential because it is part of amino acids, proteins and nucleic
acids.
</p>

<h3>THE PROBLEM WITH ATMOSPHERIC NITROGEN</h3>

<p>
Atmospheric air contains a large proportion of nitrogen gas, N₂.
However, most plants cannot use atmospheric N₂ directly to make proteins.
</p>

<p>
Nitrogen must therefore be converted into usable nitrogen-containing compounds.
</p>

<h3>MAIN PROCESSES</h3>

<ul>
  <li>Nitrogen fixation</li>
