<h2>Exhalation</h2>

<h3>DEEP NOTES</h3>

<p>
<strong>Exhalation</strong> is the movement of air out of the lungs.
</p>

<h3>STEP-BY-STEP MECHANISM</h3>

<p>
During quiet exhalation:
</p>

<p>
<strong>Step 1:</strong> The diaphragm relaxes.</p>

<p>
<strong>Step 2:</strong> It moves upward and becomes more dome-shaped.</p>

<p>
<strong>Step 3:</strong> The external intercostal muscles relax.</p>

<p>
<strong>Step 4:</strong> The ribs move downward and inward.</p>

<p>
<strong>Step 5:</strong> Thoracic volume decreases.</p>

<p>
<strong>Step 6:</strong> Pressure inside the lungs increases.</p>

<p>
<strong>Step 7:</strong> Air moves out because pressure inside the lungs becomes
greater than atmospheric pressure.</p>

