<h2>Germination: Complete Reasoning Problem</h2>

<h3>DEEP NOTES</h3>

<p>A student places viable seeds in three different conditions.</p>

<p><strong>Condition A:</strong> adequate water, oxygen and suitable temperature.</p>

<p><strong>Condition B:</strong> no water but adequate oxygen and suitable temperature.</p>

<p><strong>Condition C:</strong> water present but very little oxygen.</p>

<h3>Condition A</h3>

<p>The seeds have the main environmental conditions needed for germination.</p>

<p>Water hydrates the seed and activates metabolic processes.</p>

<p>Oxygen supports aerobic respiration.</p>

<p>A suitable temperature allows enzyme-controlled reactions to proceed effectively.</p>

<h3>Condition B</h3>

<p>Without sufficient water, normal germination cannot begin effectively.</p>

<p>The seed cannot properly activate the metabolic processes required for growth.</p>

<h3>Condition C</h3>

<p>Water is available, but very low oxygen can limit aerobic respiration.</p>

<p>This reduces the energy available for the growing embryo.</p>

<h3>Complete Reasoning Chain</h3>

<p><strong>Suitable conditions → seed becomes metabolically active → stored food is mobilised → respiration supplies energy → embryo grows → seedling develops.</strong></p>

<h3>Exam Rule</h3>

<p>When explaining germination, do not merely list "water, oxygen and warmth."</p>

<p>Explain what each condition allows the seed to do.</p>
