<p>Both develop a root and shoot.</p>

<p>Both require coordinated growth of embryonic tissues.</p>

<h3>Worked Identification</h3>

<p>Seedling A has cotyledons above the soil.</p>

<p>Seedling B has cotyledons below the soil while its shoot is above the soil.</p>

<p>Therefore:</p>

<p>A → epigeal.</p>

<p>B → hypogeal.</p>

<h3>Exam Strategy</h3>

<p>Ignore the general direction of the shoot.</p>

<p>Look specifically at the position of the cotyledons.</p>
