<h2>Calculating Germination Percentage</h2>

<h3>DEEP NOTES</h3>

<p>Germination percentage allows different groups of seeds to be compared even when the groups contain different numbers of seeds.</p>

<h3>Formula</h3>

<p><strong>Germination percentage = (number of seeds that germinated ÷ total number of viable seeds) × 100</strong></p>

<h3>Worked Example 1</h3>

<p>20 viable seeds are planted.</p>

<p>16 germinate.</p>

<p>Germination percentage:</p>

<p>(16 ÷ 20) × 100 = 80%</p>

<h3>Worked Example 2</h3>

<p>50 viable seeds are planted.</p>

<p>35 germinate.</p>

<p>(35 ÷ 50) × 100 = 70%</p>

<h3>Comparing Groups</h3>

<p>Group A has 16 germinated seeds out of 20.</p>

<p>Group B has 35 germinated seeds out of 50.</p>

<p>Although Group B has more germinated seeds in total, Group A has the higher germination percentage.</p>

<p>This is why percentage is useful when group sizes differ.</p>
