<p>A seed germinates while lying on its side.</p>

<p>After several days, the root curves downward and the shoot curves upward.</p>

<p><strong>What explains this response?</strong></p>

<p>The root shows positive gravitropism, while the shoot shows negative gravitropism.</p>

<h3>Important Point</h3>

<p>Gravitropism is a growth response, not a rapid movement of the whole plant.</p>

<p>The curvature develops because growth is unequal on different sides of the organ.</p>
