<h2>Phototropism in Shoots</h2>

<h3>DEEP NOTES</h3>

<p>Phototropism is directional growth in response to light.</p>

<p>Shoots generally show positive phototropism, meaning they grow toward a light source.</p>

<h3>Step-by-Step Explanation</h3>

<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Light comes mainly from one side.</p>

<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Auxin becomes distributed unevenly in the shoot.</p>

<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> More auxin accumulates on the shaded side of the shoot.</p>

<p><strong>Step 4:</strong> Cells on the shaded side elongate more.</p>

