<h3>Basic Investigation</h3>

<p>Place similar seedlings in controlled conditions.</p>

<p>Expose one group to light from one direction.</p>

<p>Keep other important conditions constant.</p>

<p>Observe the direction of shoot growth over time.</p>

<h3>Variables</h3>

<p><strong>Independent variable:</strong> direction or pattern of light exposure.</p>

<p><strong>Dependent variable:</strong> direction or degree of shoot bending.</p>

<p><strong>Control variables:</strong> plant species, age, water supply, temperature, growing medium and duration.</p>

<h3>Control Group</h3>

