<h2>Auxin and Root Formation in Cuttings</h2>

<h3>DEEP NOTES</h3>

<p>Auxin can promote the formation of adventitious roots in suitable plant cuttings.</p>

<p>This is one reason auxin is useful in vegetative propagation.</p>

<h3>What Is a Cutting?</h3>

<p>A cutting is a piece of plant tissue removed from a parent plant and encouraged to form a new plant.</p>

<h3>Role of Auxin</h3>

<p>Applying an appropriate auxin treatment to the base of a cutting can encourage root formation.</p>

<p>Once roots develop, the cutting can absorb water and mineral ions and become established as an independent plant.</p>

